<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <!--
        Tier 2 · Hardware. Everything in here needs a device no hosted runner
        has — today a running SteamVR and a headset — so it is in hardware.slnf
        and in no other filter.

        One project for the tier rather than one per production project. A
        folder per production project inside it is what keeps "where does this
        test live" answerable; the tier is what decides which project.

        These do not skip when the runtime is absent, the same rule Tier 3
        follows: a skip would be a green build that checked nothing. See the
        Test tiers section of docs/decisions.md. LookAtTheOverlayTests is the
        exception and skips by default, because it asserts nothing and holds the
        headset for half a minute.

        What needs no runtime lives in D47.Tier1.Tests — that the vendored
        binding loads and its entry points resolve, and what the render looks
        like as bytes before the compositor ever sees it. Both are facts a
        hosted runner can settle, and the binding tests were written precisely
        so that a mis-copied native binary is caught away from the machine with
        the headset attached.

        UseWPF is kept although this project compiles without it. What is in
        here reaches WPF only through D47.VrOverlay and D47.TestSupport, both of
        which set it, so the framework reference would arrive transitively — in
        theory. It was tried, and it built. Whether the exe still resolves the
        WPF assemblies at run time cannot be settled without SteamVR and a
        headset, and a change nobody can run is not one worth making for two
        removed lines. Drop it the next time somebody is on the dev PC with the
        runtime up and these are green.

        xUnit v3, not v2 — the SDK template still scaffolds v2, and v3 test
        projects are executables.
    -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0-windows</TargetFramework>
        <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
        <UseWPF>true</UseWPF>
        <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
        <PackageReference Include="Shouldly" />
        <PackageReference Include="xunit.v3" />
        <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\D47.VrOverlay\D47.VrOverlay.csproj" />
        <ProjectReference Include="..\D47.TestSupport\D47.TestSupport.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
